documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn6le02ob10re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Simple Past vs. Present Perfect"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Present Perfect tense to talk about a finished action or event that is connected to the present in some way. </p>  You use the Simple Past tense to talk about a finished action or event <span class=\"strong\">not</span> necessarily connected to the present."}, {"type": "text", "content": "We use <span class=\"strong\">have/has</span> + <span class=\"strong\">the past participle</span> of the verb in Present Perfect sentences."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Amelia Earhart went to an exhibition that changed her life forever."}, {"type": "example", "content": "She has managed to save enough money to buy her own plane."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The following chart shows the difference between the Simple Past and the Present Perfect."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Simple Past\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">lived</span> in Canada for two years.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">have lived</span> in Canada.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">laughed</span> when he told me the story.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">have laughed</span>.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "tex